@broadcast "Ironclad Motors - The Widowmaker Family Edition"
@category commercial
@length 30
@type commercial

::actors
@actor npc_narrator
@alias npc_narrator NARRATOR
@actor npc_car_salesman
@alias npc_car_salesman SALESMAN
::endactors

::scene TITLE

ROOM dealership_lot

EVENT FADE_IN

TITLE widowmaker_logo

MUSIC widowmaker_jingle
♪ A twangy dealership guitar riff, four chords, played like it owes someone money. ♪
MUSIC_END

::scene COMMERCIAL

CAM 1 WIDE dealership_lot

NPC npc_narrator

SHOT
A family of four walks toward a matte-grey armored transport in aggressive slow motion, hair blown by an off-camera fan.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
This year, give your family the gift of arriving.

CAM 2 CLOSEUP blast_gauge

NARRATOR:
The Widowmaker seats six, stops small-arms fire, and comes standard with an apology plaque for the trade-in.

NPC npc_car_salesman

ACTION npc_car_salesman slaps the hood twice, the universal signal of trust

SALESMAN:
Rated for whatever the road throws at you. And lately, the road throws a lot.

OVERLAY
0% APR* / AMMO INCLUDED FOR FIRST 90 DAYS

*APR REDEFINED AT DEALER'S CONVENIENCE
OVERLAY_END

CAM 3 CONTROLLED DETONATION TEST proving_ground

NPC npc_narrator

SHOT
The vehicle absorbs a modest controlled explosion; the family inside gives a thumbs-up slightly too quickly.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
The Widowmaker. Because "affordable sedan" was never going to cut it out here.

TICKER
Ironclad Motors is not responsible for the name · "Widowmaker" is a legacy trim designation and does not reflect current-year statistical outcomes · Financing subject to a background check that also checks your background's background · Detonation test performed by professionals who were compensated fairly, we are told
TICKER_END

EVENT FADE_OUT

END
